<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91835" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρρίχ-η</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχησις</span>), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>war-dance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				153
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.1.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				816b
			</span></i>; called from one <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύρριχος</span>
			the inventor, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
				<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
				46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.3.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.4.16
			</span></i>; but acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				519
			</span></i>, from its being first used at the funeral of Patroclus (from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρά</span>); as a prizecontest, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2758
			</span></i> IV (<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>), <i><span class="en">
				3089
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Teos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειναὶ
			π</span>. strange <i>contortions</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1135
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρρίχην βλέπειν</span>
			'to look daggers', <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1169
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
